PS-DGR-4: release builds compile out the collective error agreement (fold, gather, redist)
==========================================================================================
Harness: ../common. All runs against the release (non-debug) libraries.

Fold: see ../DGR-01/README: every allocation failure of dgraphFold2() (receiver or sender) and of
hdgraphFold2() hangs the other processes on pristine; returns 1 everywhere when patched.

Gather:
  ./scan.sh $WORK/pristinefi/lib ./bin_pristinefi/gatherfi 2 0 0 3 -- gather 0 5
  nth=2 exit=1 :: (0): ERROR: dgraphGatherAll2: out of memory (3); rank 0: gather rc=1; rank 1: gather rc=0
  (the processes disagree; nth=0,1 crash, see ../DGR-10/README)
  patched: nth=0..2 all ranks "gather rc=1"; nth=3 rc=0.

Redist:
  ./scan.sh $WORK/pristinefi/lib ./bin_pristinefi/redistfi 3 1 3 7 -- 0 6
  nth=3 exit=124 :: HANG; (1): ERROR: dgraphRedist: out of memory
  nth=5 exit=124 :: HANG; (1): ERROR: dgraphRedist2: out of memory (1)
  nth=6 exit=124 :: HANG; (1): ERROR: dgraphRedist2: out of memory (2)
  nth=7 exit=124 :: HANG; (1): ERROR: dgraphRedist2: out of memory (3)
  patched: nth=3,5,6,7 exit=1, all three ranks "redist rc=1".
  nth=4 hangs on both ("dgraphHaloSync2: out of memory"): dgraph_halo.c, another group's routine.
